WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.860
Speaker 1: Congresswoman Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez&nbsp;
is calling for the impeachment of Supreme Court&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:10.620
Justice Clarence Thomas over his failure to&nbsp;
disclose luxury trips paid for by a Republican&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:16.260
megadonor. We told you last week how ProPublica&nbsp;
broke this story that Thomas has been in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:23.040
pocket of right wing billionaire Harlan Crow for&nbsp;
decades. Thomas has vacationed on Crows 162 foot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:30.300
super yacht and flown on his Bombardier Global&nbsp;
5000 jet, which would have cost half a million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.820
dollars if the money had come from Thomas and he&nbsp;
had chartered it himself. The trips put Thomas in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.560
contact with corporate executives and political&nbsp;
activists, violating federal disclosure laws and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:46.080
long standing norms for a judge's conduct. This is&nbsp;
a very violation of his ethical obligations as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.640
justice, and he disregarded federal disclosure&nbsp;
laws. We were wondering if Thomas was going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.320
ever say anything at all about this because&nbsp;
he so rarely comments on anything before the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:00.000
public. But I suppose the scandal was bad enough&nbsp;
that he at least felt the need to say something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.400
about it. He said, quote. Harland and Cathy Crow&nbsp;
are among our dearest friends and we have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.500
friends for over 25 years. As friends do, we have&nbsp;
joined them on a number of family trips during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.240
the more than quarter century. We have known them.&nbsp;
Early in my tenure at the court, I sought guidance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:20.160
from my colleagues and others in the judiciary and&nbsp;
was advised that this sort of personal hospitality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.540
from close personal friends who did not have&nbsp;
business before the court was not reportable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:29.340
I have endeavored to follow that counsel&nbsp;
throughout my tenure and have always sought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:33.240
to comply with the disclosure guidelines.&nbsp;
These guidelines are now being changed as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:37.440
the Committee of the Judicial Conference&nbsp;
responsible for financial disclosure for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:42.000
the entire federal judiciary just this past&nbsp;
month announced new guidance. And it is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.580
of course, my intent to follow this guidance in&nbsp;
the future. Now, if you're as jaded and skeptical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:51.180
when it comes to politics as I am, you may&nbsp;
think that this is where the story ends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:55.020
because Thomas is basically never held&nbsp;
accountable for anything, including the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.020 --> 00:02:00.420
Anita Hill allegations, including the conflicts of&nbsp;
interest that he had with his wife, Jenny Thomas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:05.580
being a far right activist and a complete Kool-Aid&nbsp;
drinker when it comes to the conspiracy theories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:10.500
about voter fraud in the 2020 election. It seems&nbsp;
like at this point it's only Representative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:15.780
Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez who wants to do anything&nbsp;
substantial to hold Thomas accountable for these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:21.480
ethical violations. She tweeted her support for&nbsp;
impeaching Thomas late last week. And here she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:27.180
is yesterday on CNN's State of the Union with Dana&nbsp;
Bash laying out why she believes the. That Thomas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:32.040
needs to be removed from his post over this.
Speaker 5: And I believe that it is the House's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:36.660
responsibility to pursue that investigation in the&nbsp;
form of impeachment. Well, let me ask you. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:42.900
you know full well that the House is now run by&nbsp;
Republicans. How are you going to move what you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:48.900
calling for articles of impeachment through&nbsp;
a House that is run by Republicans? You know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:54.540
I think it's a it's a there is the question of&nbsp;
the politics of what we are doing, and there's the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.540 --> 00:03:01.260
question of the recourse and the accountability&nbsp;
and the structures of what we are doing. I admit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:07.440
it is a it is very difficult to see a path in&nbsp;
a Republican Party that refuses to hold itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:12.840
accountable and in fact, breaches the law itself.
Speaker 1: Now, of course, we run into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:16.980
reality that Republicans control the House&nbsp;
of Representatives, and there's basically no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:22.140
world in which Kevin McCarthy decides to introduce&nbsp;
articles of impeachment against Clarence Thomas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:27.600
at least not over this issue. But I do believe&nbsp;
it's good that there are calls for him to face an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:32.760
ethics violation, calls for him to step down, and&nbsp;
this call for him to be impeached. I do wonder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:38.340
however, if AOC is the right person to do this,&nbsp;
since she's such a polarizing figure and so many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:44.160
people are just going to write this off&nbsp;
as a radical leftist trying to attack a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:50.340
well-established Supreme Court justice over an&nbsp;
issue that maybe not impeachable in their eyes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:55.980
But even though she seems to recognize&nbsp;
that she's still deciding to be the one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:59.760
voice of reason in this matter, the one person&nbsp;
calling for impeachment and saying, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.420
if no one else is going to do it, no one else is&nbsp;
going to bring articles of impeachment forward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:07.500
I'm going to be the one to do so. Honestly,&nbsp;
this is probably the best that we can hope for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.420
right? Because Republicans rarely ever hold their&nbsp;
own accountable. You know, they're sticking by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:16.920
Donald Trump despite his criminality, despite&nbsp;
the January 6th insurrection. They're sticking by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:22.140
George Santos, despite him getting elected on the&nbsp;
basis of countless, countless lies. And they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:26.340
also going to let Clarence Thomas presumably get&nbsp;
away with this because they don't actually care&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:31.380
about integrity or rule of law or any of these&nbsp;
other things that they claim to care about, any of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:36.660
these other supposed principles that they claim to&nbsp;
espouse. I'm Pat Ford filling in for David Packman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:40.740
today. We'll be back with much more of the David&nbsp;
Pakman show right after this commercial break.

